  {
   "because": "vendor-silent",
   "blocks": [],
   "kind": "declared",
   "note": "The datasheet says 'Link and Activity LEDs per port' and the panel carries FOUR round lamps per QSFP28 port; no document maps the four (lanes 1-4, or link+activity pairs, or breakout members). HIG section 10 tables SYS, FAN, PSU0/1, ID, the FRU lamps and the RJ45 management jack, and nothing for the port lamps or the MGMT label lamp. All keep the off/on default rather than an invented vocabulary.",
   "scope": [
    "qsfp28",
    "port-leds"
   ],
   "wanted": "a per-NOS LED table from UfiSpace or a NOS vendor, or photographs of a live unit with ports in known states (down, 40G, 100G, breakout, traffic)",
   "what": "port-led-semantics"
  },
  {
   "because": "needs-drawing",
   "blocks": [],
   "kind": "declared",
   "note": "The HIG's component table gives the fan module 43.4 x 100 x 40 mm, and 43.4 matches the hex-grille section between seams in the rear renders (42.3 mm at 3.807 px/mm); but the repeating face - grille plus the flange carrying the airflow tag, captive screw (HIG Figure 15 puts both on the module) and LED - measures 50.1-50.7 mm on a 50.9 mm bay pitch. The face is modelled at the photo-measured 50.7 and the table's figure is read as the cartridge body. That reading is a judgement, not a measurement.",
   "scope": [
    "ufispace/fan-405637@1"
   ],
   "wanted": "a vendor mechanical drawing of FAN-405637 (the HIG draws dimension figures for the PSUs but none for the fan), or a caliper on the module",
   "what": "fan-faceplate-width"
  },
  {
   "because": "vendor-silent",
   "blocks": [],
   "kind": "declared",
   "note": "Neither the datasheet nor the HIG prints an orderable chassis SKU; the datasheet's 'Available to Order' section lists only PSU and fan types. A HyperScalers reseller listing names S9110-32X-2B7A, which is third-party and not carried into part-numbers.",
   "scope": [
    "chassis"
   ],
   "wanted": "a UfiSpace ordering guide or price list naming the chassis SKUs per airflow/PSU build",
